{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1127209-paths-trods-and-thorns-oh-my","id":1127209,"title":"Paths, Trods, and Thorns. Oh My!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-10T11:12:04-07:00","id":1127209,"title":"Paths, Trods, and Thorns. Oh My!","content":"The Hedge is mutable and changes. And because of that, there are so many ways that we, as STs, can portray the hedge. <br /> <br /> What I was hoping with this Topic was to see the different ways to portray the Hedge from the generic to the outlandish. I'll start of course but I did have a related question: How would someone leave the path for the Thorns? Most of how I pictured the Hedge was that it was immidiately obvious what was a path and what was not. Can the Thorns look like an offshoot path? (like a dirt path made by animals on hiking trails?)<br /> <br /> 1)<i> A vast forest of redwood-like trees extends further than the eye can see. The canopy up so high above that you could forget there was a canopy and not a very large cave. The ground is slightly damp with dew as if it was perpetually 4AM on a spring morning and the sun is ne'er present but it always seems to be soon to shine its pretty head. It never does and everything is cast in the darkness just before dawn. The darkness is exacerbated by the constant fog. Looking around, it's not like the fog is thick, rather that it's pervasive limiting eyesight and casting everything in an eerie frame. You could almost swear that something was moving out there, but no... it was likely just the wind. Wind that you don't remember feeling. One of the two most notable thing to see in this forest is the lanterns hung on red silk from a branch. Further down from the hanging lantern you can make out a soft glow that seems to indicate another hanging lantern not far from the first and its hard to see but is that another light even further? The other feature easily seen is are varying sized totem poles sparsely interspersed with the redwood-like trees with some faces almost leering in your direction, though that's prolly just a coincidence. Right?</i><br /> <br /> Following the Lanterns is the path, anything not in the direction of the Lanterns is off the path. The Thorns are simply snags of branches here and there and other sparse under-shrubbery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T11:07:27-07:00","id":1127712,"title":"","content":"2) A great, tropical river that winds and stretches for miles,occasionally splitting into a forked path every now and then. A dense jungle of trees line either side of the banks, teeming with hostile life. The river serves as the path through which to safely tread, while attempting to move on shore is considered off the path; at which point, travelers would promptly be assaulted by exaggerated versions of jungle predators and environmental hazards. Such threats include, but are not limited to giant cats, poisonous fungi, carnivorous plants, quicksand, and angry tribesmen!<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins offer ferry rides up and down the river to those willing to pay whatever strange prices are asked of them. Of course, travelers have the option to swim to their destination, but the ferrymen warn that would be inadvisable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-11-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:37:47-07:00","id":1127876,"title":"","content":"3). The path winds through a dense metropolis, sometimes in tight alleyways, some major streets. Unlike ironside streets, the place seems more like a maze vaguely designed to look like walls and doors and shopfronts, somewhat like a video-game city. Some roads dead end in illogical places, taking travelers through noticeable doors that lead to building interiors that also serve as safe paths. Trods often more closely resemble a human street or a wide open shopping mall, especially ones with many gates leading to the mortal world.<br /> <br /> Many ''decorative'' doors exist on the walls, often covered in goblin graffiti and advertisements (''buy one get half free, gogogo!'') that, to viewers, know don't continue the path. Traveling though these doors sometimes leads to a hidden Hollow, or sometimes to a goblinfruit grotto (such as a ransacked convenience store whose soda pop section is always stocked with the ever popular goblin soda ''Drink Me!''). Many of the times, it will lead off path into entirely ruined rooms littered with broken glass, sharp twisted metal and jagged shattered furniture (often covered in white sheets that billow and obscure the way forward), ultraviolet acidic black mold and mushrooms, and at least a few rooms filled with Lego pieces hard enough to feel through your shoes. Skateboards, discarded toys, sneaky ottomans, unseen corners, and the like urge wanderers to trip and stub their toes often.<br /> <br /> Dangers include: Hungry Doors that try to eat anything passing through, willowwisps appearing as distant carlights, flashlights, or radio music, Laughing Ones in the form of cabs and uber drivers, pigeon-hags hunting from guano-caked harpy nests, faerie nightclubs that distort time and can make mortals dance to death, angry smog, giant snakes that look like street lights that lie in wait standing still, and privateers resembling lost little children or confused and sexy youth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:46:31-07:00","id":1128873,"title":"","content":"4) A library bigger than you've ever seen but the Library is a lie. The Library isn't so much a physical space of a library, it is the idea of a library given form. Shelves upon shelves of objects and esoteric books of varying sizes with hallways and staircases and balconies aplenty. Not every all hall and aisle is a path though and travelers must be wary. Care observers will notice that the aisles and books and shelves are all labeled in several different manner of classifications from numbers to letters to genres and many more in signs hung from an invisible ceiling to bookmarks hung from between tomes with their labeling in big green symbols. <br /> <br /> The paths are following the labels and signs in their own order. Following the aisles Alphabetically leads to one of the largest cumulative Hollows of the Eastre Cults Freehold in Dublin where they hold their succession rites. Other paths and trods, with more and more hidden sequences lead to smaller and more specific places, and some of the paths converge on eachother such as how one would get to the front gate of Carmy's hollow: first follow the Main Trod till 'G' then take a right following only the even numbers forward and then back track the letters down from 'W' to 'S'.<br /> <br /> Not every sequence is a path, especcially the more esoteric sequences and not following a path leads the unwary wonderer to spaces where little creatures live in the shelves and snap at anything catching too close. Bits of exposed nails stick out from the ground and shelves and walls and railings and upturned metal scratches out. A Hobgoblin has become pretty devious in these parts. Only known as the Librarian, the little mouse like creature has made bank by leading those unwilling to pay its costs to the worst parts of the library.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:42:08-07:00","id":1130116,"title":"","content":"5) Mind your step. Around here, we call the Hedge the canyon with a thousand mouths, and you'd best hope that you stumble onto a road that's level and clear, else you might cut yourself up something fierce on jagged rocks and thornbushes growing gamely from every sheer surface.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the path gets so narrow that it's barely a knife's edge, suspending you over some narrow ribbon of water far below. Sometimes it widens out into a valley floor or reveals a lake, or a huge door built into the canyon wall, or a crude tunnel leading down into winding caves, or even strange cities suspended on stilts high above you.<br /> <br /> What's all the way at the top? Some folks say odd birds indeed roost there, and they're all too happy to snatch up the likes of me and you. The scavenger birds that wheel above you, preceding danger or loss, certainly must roost somewhere. Other folks say that the slopes just keep going until you reach the golden gates of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Of course, the same rumors abound regarding the caves, which are an ecosystem all their own, all blind white critters and punishing claustrophobic tunnels and wicked sharp spurs of stone, not to mention the ghosts of all the changelings and hobs who died seeking buried treasure down there in the lightless deep. As the saying goes: you haven't seen real darkness till you've been to Lost Johns' Cave.<br /> <br /> Some hobs offer their services as guides through the winding canyons, offering to take you right to your destination, or near enough, or at least in the general vicinity. Don't want to hire them? Well, enjoy trying to figure out which way to go, and what plants growing on the slopes poison on skin contact, and avoiding the scorpions of unusual size (both small enough to climb down your tear ducts and large enough to snap a minivan in half between their pincers), not to mention the roving bandit gangs, the stone-snakes, the hide-behinds, the screeching owls, the flat folk what hide on walls, the liar's grass, the thirsty mirages, and- oh, you're interested in the guided tour now, then? Single file, do whatever the guide says, and hope they don't mean to leave your bones to bleach beneath the cruel, distant sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T00:16:06-07:00","id":1130165,"title":"","content":"6) A great dance hall, far larger than any one found on earth and one which seems to be perpetually booked for a grand event of some kind. No matter when you visit, it is always a packed house, with thick crowds of dancers flourishing about on the floor. Yet there always seems to be just enough room to squeeze a few more into the writhing horde of people.<br /> <br /> This path is unique in the sense that it can only be traveled in pairs. In order to successfully navigate to the other side and find your way through danger, you and a partner must dance together, weaving in and out of the crowd in perfect synchronization. But gods help you if you should make a mistake, for the vast majority of dancers are comprised of hobgoblins, hedge beasts and True Fae.<br /> <br /> The secret is in the rhythm of the music, let it be your guide. With the music flowing through you, you shouldn't have much difficulty finding your way through the crowd. The danger happens when you disrupt the rhythm and step out of sync with the rest of the dancers. If the crowd finds out you can't follow the rhythm properly, you'll soon find yourself moving to another tune, as the floor erupts into a dance of death!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-17-2017, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}